{
 "_source": "NXT Supplier Mapping_30Jul26.xlsx, 'Source Mapping' tab — the GREEN rows only, which the workbook's own legend defines as Mapped. Yellow (Questions to NextPower), Orange (Duplicate), Blue (Oracle required but missing) and Red (Not to bring) are deliberately NOT imported.",
 "_extraction": "128 green rows read by cell fill (FF92D050), not by eye. 34 of them target 'DFF' or 'standard' rather than a named Oracle field and are excluded — a descriptive flexfield is a decision about where to put a value, not a mapping the engine can apply.",
 "_scope": "Client NextPower. Each row is keyed by SOURCE SYSTEM, so NetSuite's mapping for a field and SyteLine's are two separate learnings rather than one overwriting the other.",
 "_open_questions": [
  "Eight target fields are fed by more than one green source column for the same system: Phone (Address Phone / Phone), E-Mail (Alt. Email / Email), Tax Registration Number (CNPJ-CPF / Tax Number), Tax Organization Type (Entity Type / Is Individual), Taxpayer ID (PAN / Tax ID / Tax Id Canada), and on SyteLine Supplier Site and E-Mail. Both are seeded and the strongest-transform rule wins at apply time, but which column should govern is a business decision — confirm and I will retire the loser.",
  "29 green rows carry no Oracle page, so they are seeded against the object rather than a named interface sheet. If any belongs on one sheet only, the per-sheet scope from CW #12-14 narrows it."
 ],
